WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.719 --> 00:00:12.069
Often your password will be stored as a fixed hash value or digest.

2
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.350
So that the system can tell if your password

3
00:00:14.359 --> 00:00:17.629
matches without the password itself ever being visible.

4
00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:22.620
A more secure password with alphanumeric and special characters

5
00:00:22.629 --> 00:00:25.000
will generate a different type of hash digest.

6
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.639
However, this system of password management is already becoming obsolete.

7
00:00:30.159 --> 00:00:32.139
Often for security purposes,

8
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.419
you will be asked to generate a new password

9
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.119
with a minimum number of characters and the software

10
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.020
behind it will recognize the hash function and tell

11
00:00:40.029 --> 00:00:42.909
you if the password is sufficiently secure to be used

12
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.720
or it will prompt you to create a better password.

13
00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:50.709
Attackers can use password hashes to guess your password offline.

14
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.619
If an attacker can copy the password file,

15
00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.080
which is usually hashed from a compromised workstation or server

16
00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.400
and they know the algorithm that is used to hash the password,

17
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.650
they can use a computer to try random sequences of letters

18
00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:07.300
and number combinations to try to match the known password hash.